      <text>Solving for an unknown</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the logarithmic equation</p>

<p>\(\log_{@a@}(x)={@b@}\).</p>

<p><strong>(i)</strong> Rewrite the equation in exponential form.</p>

<p>Exponential form: \(x=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><strong>(ii)</strong> Hence, determine the value of \(x\).</p>

<p>Give your answer as an exact value.</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p><strong>Step 1: Recall the definition of a logarithm.</strong></p>

<p>The equation is \(\log_{@a@}(x)={@b@}\).</p>

<p>Recall that \(\log_a(x)=b\) is equivalent to \(x=a^b\), provided that \(a>0\), \(a\neq 1\), and \(x>0\).</p>

<p><strong>Step 2: Convert to exponential form.</strong></p>

<p>Using the definition of a logarithm, we obtain</p>

\(x={@a@}^{@b@}\).

<p><strong>Step 3: Calculate the value of \(x\).</strong></p>

<p>Substitute the given values of the base and exponent:</p>

\(x={@a@}^{@b@}={@xsol@}\).

<p><strong>Step 4: Check the solution.</strong></p>

<p>Since \({@xsol@}>0\), the logarithm is defined. Furthermore, \(\log_{@a@}({@xsol@})={@b@}\), so the solution satisfies the original equation.</p>

<p><strong>Final answer:</strong></p>

\( \boxed{x={@xsol@}} \)]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
